<newsitem itemid="204588" id="root" date="1996-11-20" xml:lang="en">
<title>UK: Dawson Intl half year profits fall.</title>
<headline>Dawson Intl half year profits fall.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>26 weeks ended September 28</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		3.1		  vs   3.8</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 1.5		  vs   1.5</p>
<p> Pretax, pre-excepts    7.3		  vs   8.4</p>
<p> Pretax		     7.3		  vs   9.0</p>
<p> Turnover		 154.3		  vs 159.6</p>
<p> Operating profit	 9.9		  vs  11.7</p>
<p> Exceptionals	     nil		  vs   0.6 credit</p>
<p> Interest		   2.8		  vs   3.3</p>
<p> Tax			  1.3		  vs   1.8</p>
<p> Pay date		   January 10, 1997</p>
<p>Div registration date  December 10  Ex-div date		December 2</p>
<p>NOTE - Chairman Derek Finlay said the bad news is behind the company although Dawson continues to operate in a tough trading environment. He said UK exports face the challenge of stronger sterling and J E Morgan has seen a slow start to the 1996/97 season.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
